From b0e3fbbf34a33af98071bc9032aa12071b79808e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajfa <3520832+ajfa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:09:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] sys16: emulate the DCU disk board and the memory boards

The Mesa disk control unit at 0xd00000 is driven at command level: three
argument bytes, an opcode, and an IOCB in main memory naming the transfer
and pointing at a table of physical page addresses.  Interface taken from
the GENIX sources (sys/dcu.h, io/dc.c, stand/dcusaio.c and dcutest.c).

With it and the full 4 MB of memory the ROM monitor boots GENIX V.2 from
disk: UNIX/2.0v1: unixsys32.
---
 src/devices/cpu/ns32000/ns32000.cpp |   5 +-
 src/mame/natsemi/sys16.cpp          | 343 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 344 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

